# Pinned game working copy — a 451 MB copy of a commercial game.
# Never tracked. Runs launch from here so the Steam install stays clean
# and the build stays pinned against Steam auto-update.
.game/

# Per-worker clones of that copy, one per concurrent match. A running game
# writes three fixed-name paths into its own directory — preferences.ini,
# saves/autosave.rwsave.tmp2 and the mod cache — so two matches sharing one
# directory race on all three. Everything else the harness needs was already
# per-invocation: the agent jar is GUID-stamped, the channel port is drawn per
# invocation, and the logs are named by the caller. Cloning the directory is
# the whole of what parallel matches require ([[harness-nodisplay]]).
.game-w*/

# Bulk run output (event streams, replays, per-session logs) — many
# and large. The monorepo root .gitignore already excludes **/runs/;
# this line is here for intent, not effect.
runs/

# The doctrine search's per-round artifacts: candidate doctrines and job
# files, written by the driver each round and frozen into that round's
# payload. Run products, not authored content — a committed round would
# read as a hand-designed arm.
doctrines/search/
sweeps/search/

# The population search's per-generation artifacts, same lifecycle.
doctrines/evolve/
sweeps/evolve/

# Wiki source archive is the OPPOSITE: every artifact a wiki page
# cites lives here and MUST be versioned, or citations break on a
# fresh clone and source-path-exists fails wholesale. The root
# .gitignore excludes *.log by pattern, so re-include explicitly.
# This works where a runs/ exception could not: *.log is a FILE
# pattern, and git can only re-include below a directory that was
# never itself excluded.
!wiki/sources/**

# Compiled agent output. The Java SOURCE under agent/src/ is tracked; the
# jar and classes are rebuilt by `make agent` and pinned to nothing.
agent/build/

# Downloaded analysis tooling (CFR decompiler and friends). Binaries, fetched
# on demand, and not ours to vendor.
.tools/

# Decompiler output, wherever it is written. A derived work of a commercial
# game: regenerable in one command, and never committed. Both spellings are
# listed because two of them have been used, and the cost of missing one is
# 1,699 files of game source in the history.
.decompiled/
decompiled/

# Python / tooling
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
# pytest's basetemp, pinned inside the repo by --basetemp so xdist workers
# share a predictable root. Test trees written here are throwaway fixtures.
.pytest_tmp/
.coverage
.env
